<article class="env-exercise" id="02CL">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02CL">Exercise <span data-tag="02CL">111.1.6</span>.</a> Algebra. (Silly and should be easy.) </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Give an example of a ring $A$ and a nonsplit short exact sequence of $A$-modules 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to M_1 \to M_2 \to M_3 \to 0.  \]
</div>
</li><li><p>
Give an example of a nonsplit sequence of $A$-modules as above and a faithfully flat $A \to B$ such that 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to M_1\otimes _ A B \to M_2\otimes _ A B \to M_3\otimes _ A B \to 0.  \]
</div>
<p>
 is split as a sequence of $B$-modules. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
